1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,689
(Sheldon:)She sounds exactly like you.

2
00:00:06,798 --> 00:00:08,628
(Amy:)How'd it go with Leonard?

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,460
(Penny:)I don't think he'll be making that mistake again.

4
00:00:11,636 --> 00:00:13,796
(Leonard:)- Good.
- So I know this goes without saying...

5
00:00:14,005 --> 00:00:17,335
(Penny:)...but if either of you tell Leonard
you helped me rewrite this paper...

6
00:00:17,509 --> 00:00:19,669
...I'll beat you both
with a bag of oranges.

7
00:00:20,011 --> 00:00:21,441
(Sheldon:)- Okay.
- Understood.

8
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:23,976
(Penny:)Now, ladies.
We got a B-minus on this paper.

9
00:00:24,182 --> 00:00:28,142
(Penny:)I think if we put our heads together,
on the next one, we could get an A.

10
00:00:28,353 --> 00:00:31,083
(Bernadette:)But we got you a B-minus on purpose
to make it believable.

11
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:32,342
(Penny:)Believable?

12
00:00:33,691 --> 00:00:34,851
(Penny:)You saying I'm not smart?

13
00:00:35,059 --> 00:00:36,549
(Penny:)- You're smart.
- No, no.

14
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:39,690
(Penny:)That's better.

15
00:00:41,733 --> 00:00:43,533
(Amy:)I feel like I'm in high school again.

16
00:00:43,735 --> 00:00:47,765
(Bernadette:)Yeah, doing the prom queen's homework
so she'll like us.

17
00:00:48,206 --> 00:00:49,726
(Howard:)I know.

18
00:00:49,974 --> 00:00:52,534
(Amy:)It's finally working.

19
00:01:03,922 --> 00:01:05,222
(Sheldon:)It's Stephen Hawking.

20
00:01:06,224 --> 00:01:08,924
Answer it. I wanna hear.

21
00:01:10,428 --> 00:01:13,128
(Sheldon:)Professor Hawking,
how nice of you to call.

22
00:01:13,331 --> 00:01:17,561
(Stephen Hawking:)Hello. I really enjoyed our game, Dr. Cooper.

23
00:01:17,769 --> 00:01:23,169
- Oh, me too.
- Or should I say, Dr. Loser?

24
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:28,411
Ha-ha-ha.

25
00:01:30,648 --> 00:01:34,348
(Sheldon:)Yes, congratulations.
You won fair and square.

26
00:01:34,586 --> 00:01:36,286
(Sheldon:)Very impressive, sir.

27
00:01:36,487 --> 00:01:40,757
- Do you like brainteasers?
- Oh, I love brainteasers.

28
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:46,699
(Stephen Hawking:)What does Sheldon Cooper
and a black hole have in common?

29
00:01:46,931 --> 00:01:49,061
(Stephen Hawking:)They both suck.

30
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:58,044
Neener-neener.

